DOCUMENT
TITLE: User Interface and Experience Requirements
UID: REQ-UI-001
VERSION: 1.0
CLASSIFICATION: Internal
REQ_TYPE: User Requirements

CONTENT
{FREE_TEXT}
This document defines the user interface and experience requirements for the web application. The interface must be intuitive, accessible, and provide an excellent user experience across all devices and platforms.

The design shall follow modern UX principles including user-centered design, progressive disclosure, and consistent interaction patterns.
{FREE_TEXT}

[SECTION]
TITLE: Design Principles
UID: REQ-UI-002
STATUS: Approved
TAGS: design, principles, ux
TITLE: User Experience Design Principles
STATEMENT: The interface shall follow user-centered design principles with focus on usability, accessibility, and user satisfaction.
RATIONALE: User-centered design ensures the application meets user needs and provides an intuitive experience that reduces learning curve and increases adoption.

REQUIREMENT
UID: REQ-UI-003
STATUS: Approved
TAGS: consistency, design-system, patterns
TITLE: Design System Consistency
STATEMENT: The interface shall maintain visual and interaction consistency through a comprehensive design system with standardized components.
RATIONALE: Consistent design reduces cognitive load, improves usability, and creates a professional brand experience.

REQUIREMENT
UID: REQ-UI-004
STATUS: In Review
TAGS: performance, loading, feedback
TITLE: Performance and Feedback
STATEMENT: The interface shall provide immediate visual feedback for user actions and maintain responsive performance under normal load conditions.
RATIONALE: Responsive feedback improves user confidence and perceived performance, while actual performance ensures smooth user experience.

[SECTION]
TITLE: Navigation and Information Architecture
UID: REQ-UI-005
STATUS: Approved
TAGS: navigation, information-architecture, structure
TITLE: Navigation Structure
STATEMENT: The application shall implement clear and intuitive navigation with breadcrumbs, search functionality, and logical information hierarchy.
RATIONALE: Clear navigation helps users find information quickly and reduces frustration, improving overall user satisfaction.

REQUIREMENT
UID: REQ-UI-006
STATUS: In Review
TAGS: search, discovery, findability
TITLE: Search and Discovery
STATEMENT: The interface shall provide advanced search capabilities with filters, sorting options, and search suggestions.
RATIONALE: Effective search functionality enables users to quickly find relevant information and improves overall productivity.

REQUIREMENT
UID: REQ-UI-007
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: breadcrumbs, navigation, context
TITLE: Contextual Navigation
STATEMENT: The interface shall display breadcrumb navigation showing user's current location within the application hierarchy.
RATIONALE: Breadcrumbs provide context and enable users to understand their location and navigate back to previous levels easily.

[SECTION]
TITLE: Responsive Design Requirements
UID: REQ-UI-008
STATUS: Approved
TAGS: responsive, mobile, adaptive
TITLE: Multi-Device Support
STATEMENT: The interface shall be fully responsive and optimized for desktop, tablet, and mobile devices with adaptive layouts.
RATIONALE: Users access applications from various devices, and responsive design ensures optimal experience regardless of screen size.

REQUIREMENT
UID: REQ-UI-009
STATUS: In Review
TAGS: touch, mobile, interaction
TITLE: Touch Interface Support
STATEMENT: The interface shall support touch interactions on mobile devices with appropriate touch targets and gesture recognition.
RATIONALE: Touch interfaces require different interaction patterns than mouse-based interfaces, and proper touch support improves mobile usability.

REQUIREMENT
UID: REQ-UI-010
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: orientation, mobile, layout
TITLE: Orientation Handling
STATEMENT: The interface shall adapt to both portrait and landscape orientations on mobile devices with appropriate layout adjustments.
RATIONALE: Users frequently rotate their devices, and proper orientation handling ensures optimal viewing experience in all orientations.

[SECTION]
TITLE: Accessibility Requirements
UID: REQ-UI-011
STATUS: Approved
TAGS: accessibility, wcag, inclusive
TITLE: Accessibility Standards
STATEMENT: The interface shall comply with WCAG 2.1 AA standards for accessibility, including keyboard navigation and screen reader support.
RATIONALE: Accessibility compliance ensures the application is usable by people with disabilities and may be legally required.

REQUIREMENT
UID: REQ-UI-012
STATUS: In Review
TAGS: keyboard, navigation, accessibility
TITLE: Keyboard Navigation
STATEMENT: All interface elements shall be accessible via keyboard navigation with logical tab order and visible focus indicators.
RATIONALE: Keyboard navigation is essential for users with motor disabilities and those who prefer keyboard-based interaction.

REQUIREMENT
UID: REQ-UI-013
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: screen-reader, assistive, technology
TITLE: Screen Reader Support
STATEMENT: The interface shall provide proper semantic markup and ARIA labels for screen reader compatibility.
RATIONALE: Screen reader support enables users with visual impairments to access and interact with the application effectively.

[SECTION]
TITLE: Form Design and Validation
UID: REQ-UI-014
STATUS: Approved
TAGS: forms, validation, user-input
TITLE: Form Design Principles
STATEMENT: Forms shall be designed with clear labels, logical grouping, and progressive disclosure to minimize cognitive load.
RATIONALE: Well-designed forms improve completion rates, reduce errors, and provide better user experience.

REQUIREMENT
UID: REQ-UI-015
STATUS: In Review
TAGS: validation, feedback, errors
TITLE: Input Validation and Feedback
STATEMENT: Forms shall provide real-time validation with clear error messages and suggestions for correction.
RATIONALE: Immediate validation feedback helps users correct errors quickly and reduces form abandonment rates.

REQUIREMENT
UID: REQ-UI-016
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: autocomplete, suggestions, efficiency
TITLE: Autocomplete and Suggestions
STATEMENT: Text input fields shall provide intelligent autocomplete and suggestions based on user history and common patterns.
RATIONALE: Autocomplete functionality improves input efficiency and reduces user effort, especially for repetitive data entry.

[SECTION]
TITLE: Data Visualization
UID: REQ-UI-017
STATUS: Approved
TAGS: visualization, charts, data
TITLE: Data Presentation
STATEMENT: The interface shall provide clear and effective data visualization using appropriate chart types and interactive elements.
RATIONALE: Effective data visualization helps users understand complex information quickly and supports data-driven decision making.

REQUIREMENT
UID: REQ-UI-018
STATUS: In Review
TAGS: interactive, charts, exploration
TITLE: Interactive Data Exploration
STATEMENT: Data visualizations shall support interactive exploration with zoom, filter, and drill-down capabilities.
RATIONALE: Interactive visualizations enable users to explore data at different levels of detail and discover insights.

REQUIREMENT
UID: REQ-UI-019
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: export, data, sharing
TITLE: Data Export and Sharing
STATEMENT: The interface shall allow users to export data visualizations in multiple formats and share them via various channels.
RATIONALE: Data export and sharing capabilities enable collaboration and integration with other tools and workflows.

[SECTION]
TITLE: Error Handling and Recovery
UID: REQ-UI-020
STATUS: Approved
TAGS: error-handling, recovery, user-support
TITLE: Error Prevention and Recovery
STATEMENT: The interface shall implement error prevention strategies and provide clear recovery options when errors occur.
RATIONALE: Good error handling reduces user frustration and helps users recover from mistakes quickly and effectively.

REQUIREMENT
UID: REQ-UI-021
STATUS: In Review
TAGS: error-messages, communication, clarity
TITLE: Error Communication
STATEMENT: Error messages shall be written in clear, user-friendly language with specific guidance on how to resolve issues.
RATIONALE: Clear error messages help users understand what went wrong and how to fix it, improving overall user experience.

REQUIREMENT
UID: REQ-UI-022
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: help, support, documentation
TITLE: Help and Support Integration
STATEMENT: The interface shall provide contextual help, tooltips, and integrated support documentation for complex features.
RATIONALE: Integrated help and support reduce user confusion and improve self-service capabilities, reducing support burden.

[SECTION]
TITLE: Personalization and Customization
UID: REQ-UI-023
STATUS: Approved
TAGS: personalization, customization, user-preferences
TITLE: User Personalization
STATEMENT: The interface shall support user personalization including customizable dashboards, themes, and layout preferences.
RATIONALE: Personalization improves user satisfaction and productivity by allowing users to adapt the interface to their specific needs and preferences.

REQUIREMENT
UID: REQ-UI-024
STATUS: In Review
TAGS: themes, appearance, branding
TITLE: Theme and Appearance Options
STATEMENT: The interface shall support multiple themes including light, dark, and high contrast modes for different user preferences and accessibility needs.
RATIONALE: Theme options accommodate different user preferences and environmental conditions, improving overall usability.

REQUIREMENT
UID: REQ-UI-025
STATUS: Draft
TAGS: dashboard, widgets, layout
TITLE: Customizable Dashboards
STATEMENT: Users shall be able to customize their dashboards by adding, removing, and rearranging widgets and information panels.
RATIONALE: Customizable dashboards enable users to focus on relevant information and optimize their workflow efficiency. 